 "title": "Place Value",
 "summary": "Learn how digit positions change values, compare decimals, and build numbers carefully from cards or written clues.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "In the number 10 we have one lot of ten and zero ones."
  },
  {
   "kind": "figure",
   "figure_ref": "assets/001-placevalue1.jpg",
   "alt": "placevalue1"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "In the number 23 we have 2 lots of ten and 3 ones. 20 + 3 = 23"
  },
  {
   "kind": "figure",
   "figure_ref": "assets/002-placevalue2.jpg",
   "alt": "placevalue2"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "In the number 59 we have 5 lots of ten and 9 ones. 50 + 9 = 59"
  },
  {
   "kind": "figure",
   "figure_ref": "assets/003-placevalue3.jpg",
   "alt": "placevalue3"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "In the number 136 we have 1 lot of 100, 3 tens and 6 ones. 100 + 30 + 6 = 136"
  },
  {
   "kind": "figure",
   "figure_ref": "assets/004-placevalue4.jpg",
   "alt": "placevalue4"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "For bigger numbers we use more and more columns. Each column is ten times bigger than the column to its right."
  },
  {
   "kind": "figure",
   "figure_ref": "assets/005-placevalue5.jpg",
   "alt": "placevalue5"
  },
  {
